		"nodes": {
			"0": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "Texture from Data\n\nThe Texture from Data node converts other types like Float and Bool to either Texture2Dchannel or Texture2Drgba types.\nWhich conversion is made depends on the input.\n\nSingle value inputs like float, int and bool will produce a Texture2Dchannel type.\nMulti-value inputs like Float2, Float3, Float4 and Color will produce a Texture2Drgba type.\n\nWhen the Texture from Data node receives a single value it will generate a single pixel texture (1x1).\nWhen it receives an instanced value it will generate a Nx1 sized texture.\nFor example: a Linear node, set to float, with 10 instances will generate a 10 x 1 pixels Texture2Dchannel.\n\nThe output of the Texture from Data node can be scaled to absolute or relative scale and be sampled either with the nearest or linear sampling mode. Sampling and Bit Depth can be exposed as attribute inlets too."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 303.63323974609375,
					"width": 818.006591796875,
					"x": 315.777313232421875,
					"y": 142.6087646484375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
